      "writtenOn": "2018-05-02T02:17:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right.\n\n\n1）requestDeathNotification() called by linkToDeath() left BINDER_WORK_DEAD_BINDER in thread-\u003etodo because target process has died.  using flush command， no need read from binder driver.\n2) attachApplicationLocked() left BINDER_WORK_RETURN_ERROR in thread-\u003etodo as target process has died.\n3) Client pick up BINDER_WORK_DEAD_BINDER in the head of thread-\u003etodo, then add BR_DEAD_BINDER to mIn buffer.\n4) Death recipient called by reportOneDeath() pick up BINDER_WORK_RETURN_ERROR which is producted by attachApplicationLocked()\n5) Oneway attachApplicationLocked() can be blocked forever.",
      "parentUuid": "2311dd53_a0a7045d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 45
      },
